\section{The floor, which matters with few donors}{
The smallest attainable p-value is \code{1/n_units}: even a treated unit that
out-ranks every placebo gets \code{1/n}, never zero. With 40 units that floor
is 0.025, and a p-value of 0.05 means "second largest of forty", not
"significant at five percent" in the usual sampling sense. Read these as
ranks, and do not report them to three decimals as if they were
continuous.
